It was a long time ago... about 70529 turns ago a brand new Human
Ranger called Davy
found the entrance of the Mazes of Menace. That sounded dreadful, but
he was a promising
character with his 18 COS. Davy knew from reading the
rec.games.roguelike.nethack that
ranged weapons were his salvation on his way to eternal lifehood.

On DL3, at XL1 he gained Poison resistance eating a red mold corpse,
then a goblin left
a pair of elven boots... stealthy!

On his way to Minetown he found the first bonefile, where a ranger had
found an orrible
death from a giant ant i believe. ( --> a lot of cursed +2 arrows )
Minetown altar was neutrally aligned, it's a matter of luck!

No magic lamps anyway... never mind.
He came back to main dungeon and on DL4 found an altar, converted it
and obtained some holy
water he used to bless a smoky potion... Blessed +2 gray dragon scale
mail. It just started
to be an interesting game. Arrows in the early game kick asses and
AC=3D-6!

Went back in the mines and found 2 arrows traps, when arrows were
becoming too few.
Lucky again. And here is the second bonefile of a wizard who was
wielding MagicBane and carrying
2 scrolls of identify --> i had already a luckstone!

That was the moment i realized i hadn't fire, sleep and shock
resistances yet.
Being killed while helpless would have been a pity.
In the meanwhile Venus gave me the Mjollnir, which i nearly didn't use
the whole game.
After having obtained sleep res by the 4th elf corpse, i went down to
Medusa.
I had a ring of levitation, which was polverised in the middle of the
sea by an eletric eel...

DYWYPI?

Well, no, because my amulet crumbled to dust and i was actually
teleported in Medusa's island!!!
LUCKYLUCKYLUCKY! I had no means of levitation, but i had a wand of fire
and decided to
get down to the castle. Again, a bugle and rec.games.roguelike.nethack
helped Davy.
Opened the bridge, and while killing everything that moved Davy gained
Shock resistance
from a tasty Storm giant.

-->WoW-->

